{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThis 18-path tests/scripts cohort has 53 editable prose blocks. The retired inventory had 39; the immutable-basis census adds 14 blocks in dependency-audit and observability tests.\n\nBefore-citations and inventory are pinned to origin/main@0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e. At repair time origin/main was 10533b1e3f651a60e8cea5691318c108ff1f3396; its intervening workflow/grounding changes did not touch these paths. Implement from current origin/main, but retain 0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e as the prose-audit basis. The leaf change is one commit, so changed-path checks use HEAD^..HEAD.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only ordinary comments/docstrings at these stable module, symbol, or prose-first-line anchors. Do not edit code, assertions, directives, runtime strings, _stub(...) payloads, or unlisted prose.\n\nFor each Python path, parse base/final text with ast.parse(source, type_comments=True); recursively remove only the leading Expr(Constant(str)) from Module, ClassDef, FunctionDef, and AsyncFunctionDef bodies; normalize only ast.TypeIgnore.lineno; and require exact ast.dump(..., include_attributes=False) equality. Separately compare directives because comments are absent from the AST.\n\nA non-author reviewer posts exactly 53 TSV rows:\npath<TAB>anchor/kind<TAB>before-citation<TAB>after-citation<TAB>preserved-contract-or-consumer<TAB>before-words<TAB>after-words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer-session\nCitations use full immutable before/final SHAs. Both verdicts must be PASS; missing rows block closure.\n\n## Scope — 53 blocks\n- test_check_config_reads_red_proof.py — module; scoped old_gate prose; test_the_pre