t_not_enforcing_is_not_offered; comment before test_ambient_ci_does_not_waive_the_sandbox; test_the_sandboxed_subprocesses_receive_the_hardened_env docstring; comment before _is_mutmut_run. Preserve containment, child-liveness, capability probes, hardened env, and whole-module binding.\n- test_normalize_ci_conclusion.py — module docstring; preserve two-input normalization/closed output.\n- test_observability_coldstart_e2a6.py — module; _environment cursor comment; _state docstring; seed comment in test_cold_start_publishes_zero_and_seeds_the_offset. Preserve publish-before-persist, cursor state, and the bare-total log exception.\n- test_observability_data_disk_debris.py — module docstring; preserve non-site census, real du, bounded dimensions, and no fabricated zero.\n- test_observability_disk_pressure.py — module; _environment cursor comment; _state_total, test_real_markers_are_counted_alongside_the_prose, and test_no_persistence_markers_publishes_zero docstrings. Preserve record anchoring, ineffective-reclaim persistence, and separate scratch-mount signal.\n- test_observability_exit.py — module docstring; preserve aggregate exit-zero with visible individual failures.\n- test_observability_marker_anchor_8c2f.py — module; _environment cursor comment; test_offsets_inflated_by_false_counts_cannot_distort_a_delta docstring and inline inflated-total comment. Preserve cursor immunity to inflated legacy totals, not obsolete \"lost-history clamp\" wording.\n- test_observability_mcp_health_9ea3.py — module plus test_an_unhealthy_serving_path_publishes_zero_not_nothing and test_upstream_lost_mid_gate_latches_a_sustained_zero docstrings. Preserve 401-as-healthy, explicit bad-path zero, and serving-path independence.\n- test_observability_mcp_markers.py — module; _environment cursor comment; cold-start seed comment in test_cold_start_seeds_offsets_and_publishes_zero. Preserve separate retire-cap/memory-abort counters.\n\nThe 14 additions are dependency_audit +5, coldstart_e2a6 +3, disk_pressure +2, marker_anchor_8c2f +2, and mcp_markers +2.\n\n## Consumers / exclusions\nPytest consumes all 18 modules; scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py consumes prose deterministically. No targeted __doc__, inspect.getdoc, or doctest consumer was found.\n\nObservability tests import tests/scripts/_journald_stub.py, but it is outside the parent's retired boundary and must not enter file impact. Its JOURNALCTL_EMULATOR/TIMEOUT_STUB and every scoped _stub(...) multiline string are runtime content. No directives exist in the 18 paths; the directive signature must stay empty.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Only the 53 anchors or adjacent blank lines change, and every edited block is shorter/current.\n- [ ] Normalized ASTs exactly match 0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e; runtime payloads remain identical.\n- [ ] The directive signature remains empty.\n- [ ] HEAD^..HEAD changes exactly the 18 file-impact paths and excludes _journald_stub.py.\n- [ ] The non-author TSV has exactly 53 PASS/PASS rows with full SHAs.\n- [ ] All seven structured semantic, directive, path, diff, hygiene, focused-test, and make-verify checks pass.\n\n## Verification\nRun every structured verify command. Automated guards prove structure; the independent TSV is authoritative for prose quality. The focused command executes all scoped files, including the new dependency-audit nodes and renamed marker test."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788619022963326790,"uuid":"5685f3cc-4a30-4684-a08e-8675dd81f648"}